**FOLLOW:** This fix changes the set of constants available for grounding in `_verify_z3_v2_shadow`. Claims that previously matched inner‑scope constants will now fail to ground, potentially increasing UNCERTAIN verdicts. This is correct behavior (prevents false proofs), but may reduce the coverage of the B‑Cell v2. No other functions call `_extract_constants_from_ast`; the only downstream impact is on `_verify_z3_v2_shadow` and its callers (`b_cell_v2_shadow`). The shadow log will show fewer “grounded” proofs, which should be reviewed for false positives. The fix also requires adding a `parent` attribute to AST nodes (safe as we only attach during visitation).
